This project is an independent Rust implementation of an Oblivious HTTP
(RFC 9458) gateway, built to the RFC directly rather than as a port of any
other implementation. It contains no source code copied from Cloudflare's
`privacy-gateway-server-go`, and its design and feature set have since
diverged from and in several respects gone beyond it (native X-Wing rather
than a draft KEM, optional direct mTLS, RFC-9458-aligned status codes,
hardened outbound URL/Host handling, multi-generation key rotation).

One specific behavior is a deliberate, narrow exception: this project's
X25519 key derivation reproduces `privacy-gateway-server-go`'s legacy
derivation input byte-for-byte (see `GLOSSARY.md`), so an operator who
reuses an existing seed keeps the same public key for clients that already
embed or cache it. This project also uses the same BSD-3-Clause license as
that project, as a deliberate choice, not because any of its code was
reused:

