Third-party Rust crate dependency licenses were reviewed via `cargo
metadata` against the locked dependency graph (`Cargo.lock`). Every
dependency declares a permissive license (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2/3-Clause,
ISC, Zlib, Unicode-3.0, CDLA-Permissive-2.0, BSL-1.0, or Unlicense, in
various dual/multi-license combinations); none are copyleft. This is an
enforced CI gate, not just a one-time manual check: `deny.toml` encodes
the same allow-list, and the `deny` job in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs
`cargo deny check licenses`, `check bans sources`, and (soft-gated,
`continue-on-error`) `check advisories` on every push and pull request.
Run it locally with:

    cargo deny check licenses
    cargo deny check bans sources
    cargo deny check advisories

